wildos-archive (0.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The search box has the right-click menu with Cut, Copy, Paste and
    Select all. The Menu key and Shift+F10 open it too.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:54:22 +0000

wildos-archive (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Opens password-protected 7z and RAR archives, hidden file names
    included: Archive asks for the password, then lists, extracts, tests
    and shows pictures from them. 7-Zip reads protected 7z, The
    Unarchiver protected RAR 5; libarchive still reads everything else.
  * The password never goes on a command line or to disk.
  * Files from 7-Zip and The Unarchiver are unpacked into a private
    folder first and only then moved into place, with the same checks as
    every other archive: nothing lands outside the folder you chose.
  * RAR files protected with the older RAR 4 encryption say so plainly.
    No free tool can unlock them yet.
  * The icon ink in light mode is the warm grey of the rest of Wild OS.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0000

wildos-archive (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Extract here asks before extracting into a folder that is already
    there: replace its files or keep both.
  * The Extract here progress window opens at its full size instead of
    as a thin strip.

